  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 239 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nDry weather with near normal temperatures is forecast Wednesday \nthrough Thursday thanks in part due to a weak ridge of surface high \npressure across the area. We are still looking for a good chance (50-\n70%) of showers and thunderstorms from a potential MCS Thursday \nnight - Friday night. Ensemble guidance has shifted a bit more \ntoward a slower midlevel trough passage this weekend, with a \nminority (23%) of members from the LREF showing a cutoff midlevel \nlow. This means a couple of things, but namely: 1) cooler daytime \ntemperatures Friday through next weekend and 2) lingering rain \nchances.",
